-**Logic per tile:** the ALU and comparator, the 128 × 64-bit true dual-port register file, two adders (memory address, pc + imm), the operand resolver, the decode index logic, three queue readers and the credit counters: about 0.1–0.15 mm² with its memories [estimate]. Section 11 adds it to the tile's budget; its placement is in section 12.
+*(Owner, 2026-10-26, part D.)* **Every tile has the same small UART.** Only a tile whose pins are wired to a serial port uses it: C&C's, once C&C is a tile (item 82). Every compute tile's is unwired.
