+### 2.9 `UART_`: the UART
+
+<!-- generated: reg UART_TX UART_RX UART_STATUS UART_DIVISOR -->
+<!-- end generated -->
+
+Every tile has the same small UART (spec 4.20), 8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit, with 16-byte TX and RX FIFOs. **Only a tile wired to a serial port uses it** (C&C's, once C&C is a tile); on every compute tile the registers decode but do nothing.
+
+| register | offset | |
+|---|---|---|
+| `UART_TX` | `0x8B0` (W) | [7:0] pushed into the TX FIFO; **the store stalls while it is full** (on an unwired tile: dropped, never stalls) |
+| `UART_RX` | `0x8B4` (R) | [7:0] the oldest byte, [8] valid; pops only when valid, and returns valid = 0 with the FIFO empty |
+| `UART_STATUS` | `0x8B8` (R/W) | [4:0] TX occupancy, [12:8] RX occupancy, [16] RX overrun, [17] framing error; reads have no side effects; write 1 to [16] or [17] to clear it |
+| `UART_DIVISOR` | `0x8BC` (R/W) | [15:0] reference-oscillator cycles per bit; takes effect at the next idle point of each direction; reset = 57,600 baud |
+
+- **Wake events,** both live, mask bits reset to 0: `WAKE_EVENTS` **[21] RX not empty** and **[22] TX not full** (2.6). On an unwired tile TX not full is always 1 and RX not empty never is.
+- **Errors drop the byte:** a byte arriving to a full RX FIFO sets overrun; a bad stop bit sets framing error.
+- **HALT doesn't reset the UART;** chip reset empties its FIFOs, clears the errors and restores the divisor.
+- **In meshsim,** every tile's `UART_TX` bytes go to that tile's console log, wired or not: `putchar` for debugging on any tile.
 
